Summary: Diablo II: Resurrected: leave out the DXVK and DXMT DLL paths
Category: graphics
Kind: workaround
Origin: reconstructed
  Version: Sikarugir 10.0_8
  Binary: WS12WineSikarugir10.0_8 ntdll.so
  Functions: set_dll_path (inlined into init_paths, 0x1e4b3-0x1e760)
  Changes: none: the same rules as 10.0_8
  Note: Sikarugir-only: no CrossOver 26, wine-staging or WineHQ equivalent
Upstream: no
Why: Diablo II: Resurrected (D2R.exe, matched by substring on argv[1]) never
 gets the WINEDLLPATH_DXVK or WINEDLLPATH_DXMT folders (unconditionally, as
 in 10.0_8), and also skips WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL when
 SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D is set, so it runs on Wine's own d3d12 (vkd3d)
 and dxgi instead. Shown on 10.0 build0 with a program named D2R.exe.
Programs: Diablo II: Resurrected (D2R.exe): presumably because it uses
 Direct3D 12, which DXVK and DXMT don't provide, while their dxgi.dll would
 replace the one Wine's d3d12 needs
Matches: exe D2R.exe
Enable: see ntdll-renderer-dll-paths (WINEDLLPATH_DXVK or WINEDLLPATH_DXMT set)
 env SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D=<anything> (D2R.exe also skips WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL)
Known issues: SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D is tested for presence only (any value,
 even "0", counts), as in 10.0_8.
Uncertain: why Sikarugir does this: 10.0_8 doesn't record a reason (Programs
 gives the likely one).
Expects before it: ntdll-renderer-dll-paths, ntdll-launcher-metal-hud (context)
No test: none written yet; a D2R.exe copy of renderer-dll-paths' program under
 WINEDLLPATH_DXVK, which must get Wine's d3d11, would cover it
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: diff context refreshed for ntdll-launcher-metal-hud's
 change; code as in build0

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -407,18 +407,33 @@ static BOOL is_launcher_process(void)
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/* Sikarugir: Diablo II: Resurrected runs on vkd3d rather than DXVK or DXMT, and
+ * also rather than D3DMetal when SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D is set */
+static BOOL is_d2r_process(void)
+{
+    return main_argc >= 2 && strstr( main_argv[1], "D2R.exe" );
+}
+
+enum d2r_rule
+{
+    D2R_USE,             /* used for D2R */
+    D2R_SKIP,            /* never used for D2R */
+    D2R_SKIP_IF_FORCED,  /* not used for D2R if SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D is set */
+};
+
 /* Sikarugir: per-renderer DLL directories, searched before the builtin ones */
 static const struct
 {
     const char *var;
     BOOL skip_for_launchers;
+    enum d2r_rule d2r;
 } renderer_dll_paths[] =
 {
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL", TRUE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_CNCD",     FALSE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_D9VK",     TRUE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXVK",     TRUE },
-    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXMT",     FALSE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL", TRUE,  D2R_SKIP_IF_FORCED },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_CNCD",     FALSE, D2R_USE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_D9VK",     TRUE,  D2R_USE },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXVK",     TRUE,  D2R_SKIP },
+    { "WINEDLLPATH_DXMT",     FALSE, D2R_SKIP },
 };
 
 static BOOL use_renderer_dll_path( unsigned int idx )
@@ -436,6 +451,17 @@ static BOOL use_renderer_dll_path( unsigned int idx )
         }
         return FALSE;
     }
+    switch (renderer_dll_paths[idx].d2r)
+    {
+    case D2R_USE:
+        break;
+    case D2R_SKIP_IF_FORCED:
+        if (!getenv( "SIKARUGIR_D2R_FORCE_VKD3D" )) break;
+        /* fall through */
+    case D2R_SKIP:
+        if (is_d2r_process()) return FALSE;
+        break;
+    }
     return TRUE;
 }
 
